---
const homophones = [
  ["there", "their", "place / belonging to them"],
  ["your", "you’re", "possession / you are"],
  ["to", "too", "direction / also"],
  ["allowed", "aloud", "permitted / out loud"]
];

const confusing = [
  ["accept / except", "accept = agree to; except = excluding"],
  ["affect / effect", "affect = influence; effect = result"],
  ["practice / practise", "practice is the noun; practise is the verb"],
  ["principle / principal", "principle = a rule; principal = the headteacher"],
  ["stationary / stationery", "stationary = still; stationery = writing paper"]
];
---

<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>Homophones - Sound and spelling</h1>
  <section class="summary-block summary-blue">
    <h2>Homophones</h2>
    <p>Homophones sound the same, but the meaning and the spelling are different.</p>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-feature" scope="col">Word</th>
          <th class="th-rule" scope="col">Sounds the same</th>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Meanings</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          homophones.map(([first, second, meaning]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{first}</th>
              <td>{second}</td>
              <td>{meaning}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>“Which word correctly completes the sentence?” They forgot to take <strong>their</strong> coats.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="summary-block summary-pink">
    <h2>Confusing words</h2>
    <p>Some words look or sound similar, but the meaning or the spelling is different.</p>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-feature" scope="col">Pair</th>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Difference</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          confusing.map(([pair, difference]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{pair}</th>
              <td>{difference}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>In proofreading, spot the word that is spelled wrongly or used wrongly.</p>
    <p>Practise word families from the same root: decide → decision → decisive.</p>
  </section>
</div>
